# Seeds of the adjudication corpus on which the decision-graph adjudicator
# intentionally differs from the iterative adjudicator that recorded
# adjudication_corpus.golden. Each line gives the seed, the category and the
# digests of the current resolution (turn 1, turn 2). The previous result
# depended on the order of its iterations in every case below; the categories
# are:
#
# cut_supporters       Report only. A supporter dislodged during the turn is
#                      listed in the combat's cut supporters; the previous
#                      adjudicator listed it only when the turn resolved in a
#                      single iteration.
# paradox              No resolution satisfies the rules: the cycle keeps the
#                      status quo. The previous adjudicator kept a
#                      dislodgement or a failure from an earlier iteration.
# legacy_inconsistent  The previous result violated the rules: an attack
#                      turned back before a head-to-head loser stopped
#                      contesting its destination, or a dislodgement kept from
#                      an earlier iteration. The current result is the
#                      consistent one.
# two_resolutions      Two resolutions satisfy the rules; the orders succeed in
#                      the adjudicator's fixed order whenever one allows it.
